; Clamacs-FPU -- double-click launcher (run by C:IconX, see Clamacs-FPU.info).
; Starts the editor/IDE on the hard-float AmigaOS 3 build: bin/aos3-fpu/clamiga
; restored from the clamacs.img next to it (the editor, already loaded) and
; told to run it.  REQUIRES a 68881/68882 FPU or a 68040/68060 with its FPU
; library (see README-FIRST, "Which AmigaOS binary?"); without one use the
; Clamacs icon.  The clamiga the editor starts for its REPL is PROGDIR:clamiga,
; i.e. the same hard-float binary.  On MorphOS the native build is the one to
; run, as the Clamacs icon does.  Needs MUI 3.8+ and TextEditor.mcc 15.29+.
; Files to edit go after `--' when started from a shell; S:.clamacsrc is
; loaded first.
Stack 131072
If EXISTS SYS:MorphOS
  Run >NIL: bin/mos/clamiga --image bin/mos/clamacs.img --heap 8M --non-interactive --eval "(clamacs::run)"
Else
  Run >NIL: bin/aos3-fpu/clamiga --image bin/aos3-fpu/clamacs.img --heap 8M --non-interactive --eval "(clamacs::run)"
EndIf
